525-b5b5-3366502ad4d8"><span hidden=""></span><div data-selected-text-overlay-target="_r_21t_" dir="auto" data-markdown-text-style="assistant-message" class="MarkdownRoot-rZKhxa [&amp;&gt;*:first-child]:mt-0 [&amp;&gt;*:last-child]:mb-0 [&amp;&gt;*:last-child]:mb-0 [&amp;&gt;ol:first-child]:mt-0 [&amp;&gt;ul:first-child]:mt-0" style="--markdown-link-color: currentColor;"><p class="Paragraph-kKnbIo" dir="auto"><span>You </span><strong class="font-semibold"><span>can technically merge while the Python program is running</span></strong><span>, because Git and the Python process are separate.</span></p><p class="Paragraph-kKnbIo" dir="auto"><span>But I </span><strong class="font-semibold"><span>don't recommend merging yet</span></strong><span>. Let </span><span data-markdown-copy="inline-code" class="inline-markdown InlineMarkdownIsolate-QWDV4W" dir="ltr">documentation_consistency.py</span><span> finish first because it may still be writing:</span></p><div class="CodeBlock-zu1QM3"><div data-markdown-copy="code-block" class="relative w-full min-w-0 overflow-clip contain-inline-size rounded-(--radius-3xl-base) border border-subtle bg-secondary-soft-alpha Surface-dfq13n dark @container" data-theme="dark" data-search-result-target=""><div data-markdown-copy="exclude" class="flex items-center font-sans text-sm select-none min-h-12 gap-2 py-1.5 ps-4 pe-1.5 font-medium text-default md:ps-5 sticky z-10 StickyActionBar-XvAQxh"><svg aria-hidden="true" class="Icon-X4VkKC" focusable="false" height="20" viewBox="0 0 20 20" width="20" xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg"><path d="M4.46951 6.27289C4.68734 5.97727 5.10354 5.91356 5.3992 6.13129C5.69464 6.34921 5.75762 6.76637 5.53982 7.06195L3.32791 10.0639L5.5369 13.0131C5.75668 13.3071 5.69695 13.7237 5.40311 13.9438C5.10923 14.1637 4.69261 14.1037 4.47244 13.81L2.04178 10.5639C1.82214 10.2704 1.8206 9.86789 2.03787 9.57269L4.46951 6.27289Z" fill="currentColor"></path> <path d="M14.6053 6.13129C14.9009 5.9136 15.3171 5.97728 15.5349 6.